  "reasoning": [
    "agentRunClaim uses the existing run resolver, computes sealVerified with the existing canonical hash/auditor-public-key-history verifier, and passes that actual boolean to envelopeForStoredRun. It no longer reaches the raw diagnostic adapter through loadDomainEvidence.",
    "The canonical stored-run adapter treats 1.1.1 or absent/unparsable old version metadata as legacy self-reported; current verified reports retain their established claim; current unverified VALID reports are evaluated as INVALID and explicitly self-reported. Resolution/shape/verification errors are caught and yield a not-evaluated unbound claim.",
    "The diagnostic stored-run path supplies neither approved independent reviewer state nor a pinned reviewer issuer. The canonical eligibility decision requires both, so an auditor seal alone does not promote the result to independently_reviewed.",
    "withClaim remains byte-identical: original first text block stays intact, canonical label remains a separate second text block, and structuredContent still merges supplied result fields with canonical claim fields. amcMcpServer is byte-identical, preserving factory/tool inventory and original text producers.",
    "The latest saved standard-parser run genuinely passes every 23 existing SDK case with zero failures, pending, todo. It checks exact 11 default tools, original ten successful tool outputs, legacy parity, current sealed/unsealed controls, licensed own-key refusals, unpaid refusal, missing/empty controls and the incident extension.",
    "The actual shared-helper mutation removes text labels and structuredContent while preserving original result text; its saved run has 16 genuine failures of 23, zero pending/todo. Restored source hash matches the reviewed source, and the later 23-case standard-parser run is green.",
    "The badge tests invoke the real HTML string renderer for four explicit canonical helper projections, neutral not-evaluated reasons, legacy wording, tooltip/attribute escaping and the shared legend. Their own comment truthfully labels reviewer/independence values as projections, not attestations."
  ],
